agm-0974: AGM H6 direct scanout through the Unisoc DPU. The GPU pool moves
below 4 GB (the DPU's layer address is 32 bits): 0xb8000000-0xdc000000, RAM between the
oemcrypto and widevine carve-outs of the stock DT that nothing here uses; the kernel gets its
5.75 GB back (mkadt.py). SweetFramebuffer drives the DPU (r6p0, 0x31000000, registers after the
vendor dpu_r5p0.c: qogirl6 has r5p0) where u-boot left it scanning the boot framebuffer in video mode with its MMU
off: a window-server frame from the pool is shown by pointing the layer at it (DPU_CTRL REG_UPDATE bit 2,
taken at vsync, UPDATE_DONE in INT_RAW 0x1ec bit 4): no copy, no tearing. Panics point it
back at the boot framebuffer. Boot-arg agm_dpu=0: frames copied as before.


